#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=12 nAlgorithms=8;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1790950824724'; [Fri Oct 02 16:20:24 CEST 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.), (Hayamizu et al, 2026 ; M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation).
The original input consisted of 17 taxa and 17 DNA sequences of length 951.
After removal of one taxon, the input consisted of 16 taxa and 16 DNA sequences of length 40.
After removal of 911 characters, the input had 40 characters.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 22 nodes and 27 edges.
The TCS Haplotype Network method (Templeton et al 1992, Leigh & Bryant 2015) was used (default options) so as to obtain 20 nodes and 22 edges.
The Simplify Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 21 nodes and 23 edges.

References:
Hayamizu et al, 2026: M. Hayamizu, others, DH Huson, in preparation
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
Leigh & Bryant 2015: J.W. Leigh and D. Bryant. PopART: full-feature software for haplotype network construction. Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 6(9):1110-1116, 2015.
Templeton et al 1992: A.R. Templeton, K.A. Crandall and C.F. Sing. A cladistic analysis of phenotypic associations with haplotypes inferred from restriction endonuclease mapping and DNA sequence data. III. Cladogram estimation. Genetics, 132(2):619-633, 1992.
]

